// WRC where the chain is carried by release/acquire synchronisation.
//
// rmm-zoo property: mca (Atomicity) -- negative control.
// Source: Lahav et al., "Taming Release-Acquire Consistency" (POPL 2016).
//
// Release-acquire synchronisation is transitive (hb is), so the acquire in P2
// inherits P0's write through P1: the stale read of x is forbidden by every
// model in the release-acquire family, multicopy atomic or not. This is the
// negative control for WRC+data+addr.lit -- it shows that the MCA question is
// about ordering by dependency, not about ordering as such.
//
// Reference verdicts: WRA, RA, SRA, C11, RC11, SC all FORBID.
x := 0;
y := 0;
{
  x.store(1, rel)
} ||| {
  r1 := x.load(acq);
  y.store(1, rel)
} ||| {
  r2 := y.load(acq);
  r3 := x.load(acq)
}
%%
forbid (r1 = 1 && r2 = 1 && r3 = 0) [RA]
